The genealogy of Jesus.
This is a record of the lineage of Jesus Christ. He is the son of David. He is also the son of Abraham.
Abraham was the father of Isaac. Isaac was the father of Jacob. Jacob was the father of Judah and his brothers.
Judah was the father of Perez and Zerah. Their mother was Tamar. Perez was the father of Hezron. Hezron was the father of Ram.
Ram was the father of Amminadab. Amminadab was the father of Nahshon. Nahshon was the father of Salmon.
Salem was the father of Boaz. Rahab was the mother of Boaz. Boaz was the father of Obed. Ruth was the mother of Obed. Obed was the father of Jesse.
And Jesse was the father of King David. And David was the father of Solomon. And the mother of Solomon was Bathsheba.
Solomon was the father of Rehoboam. Rehoboam was the father of Abijah. Abijah was the father of Asa.
Asa was the father of Jehoshaphat. Jehoshaphat was the father of Joram. Joram was the father of Ahaz.
Israel was the father of Jephthah; Jephthah was the father of Ibzan; Ibzan was the father of Elon; Elon was the father of Abdon. Abdon was the father of Eliab; Eliab was the father of Bikri; Bikri was the father of Uzzi; Uzzi was the father of Zerah; Zerah was the father of Shimei. Shimei was the father of Gog; Gog was the father of Magog; Magog was the father of Madai; Madai was the father of Elishah; Elishah was the father of Tarshish; Tarshish was the father of Rhodanim. Rhodanim was the father of Jobab; Jobab was the father of Zarephath; Zarephath was the father of Eblim; Eblim was the father of Obadah; Obadah was the father of Elah; Elah was the father of Job. Job was the father of Dardanus; Dardanus was the father of Lestes; Lestes was the father of Aphrodite. Aphrodite was the mother of Myrrha; Myrrha was the mother of Aeneas; Aeneas was the father of Romulus. Romulus was the father of Horatius. Horatius was the father of Curiatius. Curiatius was the father of Atilius. Atilius was the father of Poplicola. Poplicola was the father of Valerius. Valerius was the father of Horatii. Horatii was the father of Curiatii. Curiatii was the father of Atilii. Atilii was the father of Poplicolae. Poplicolae was the father of Valerii. Valerii was the father of Horationum. Horationum was the father of Curiationum. Curiationum was the father of Atiliationum. Atiliationum was the father of Poplicolana. Poplicolana was the father of Valerianum. Valerianum was the father of Horatianon. Horatianon was the father of Curiatonon. Curiatonon was the father of Atilatonon. Atilatonon was the father of Poplicolanum. Poplicolanum was the father of Valerianum. Valerianum was the father of Horatianum. Horatianum was the father of Curiatonum. Curiatonum was the father of Atiliationum. Atiliationum was the father of Poplicolanae. Poplicolanae was the father of Valerianon. Valerianon was the father of Horatiananon. Horatiananon was the father of Curiatonanon. Curiatonanon was the father of Atilatonanon. Atilatonanon was the father of Poplicolananon. Poplicolananon was the father of Valeriananon. Valeriananon was the father of Horatiananon. Horatiananon was the father of Curiatonanon. Curiatonanon was the father of Atilatonanon. Atilatonanon was the father of Poplicolananon. Poplicolananon was the father of Valeriananon. Valeriananon was the father of Horatiananon. Horatiananon was the father of Curiatonanon. Curiatonanon was the father of Atilatonanon. Atilatonanon was the father of Poplicolananon. Poplicolananon was the father of Valeriananon. Valeriananon was the father of Horatiananon. Horatiananon was the father of Curiatonanon. Curiatonanon was the father of Atilatonanon. Atilatonanon was the father of Poplicolananon. Poplicolananon was the father of Valeriananon. Valeriananon was the father of
Hezekiah was the father of Manasseh. Manasseh was the father of Amon. Amon was the father of Josiah.
Josiah was the father of Jonathan and his brothers. And in that time, the Jewish people were forced to leave for Babylon.
After that, the family line continued. Jehoiachin was the father of Shealtiel. Shealtiel was the father of Zerubbabel.
Zerubbabel was the father of Abiud. Abiud was the father of Eliakim. Eliakim was the father of Azor.
Azur was the father of Zadok. Zadok was the father of Akim. Akim was the father of Eliud.
Elioenai was the father of Eleazar. Eleazar was the father of Mattenai. Mattenai was the father of Jacob.
Jacob was the father of Joseph. Joseph was the husband of Mary. And Mary gave birth to Jesus, who is called the Christ.
So there were 14 generations from Abraham to David. And there were 14 from David until the Jewish people had to leave for Babylon. And there were 14 from that time to Christ. The birth of Jesus Christ
Thus Jesus Christ was born. The mother of Jesus, Mary, and her husband, Joseph, were promised in marriage. But before they began to live together, it became clear that she was pregnant. She conceived through the power of the Holy Spirit.
Her husband, Yusuf, was a pious man. He did not want to shame her publicly. So he decided to divorce her quietly.
But while Joseph was pondering this, an angel of the Lord appeared to him in a dream. The angel said, "Joseph, son of David, do not be afraid to take Mary into your home as wife, for the child in her womb is from the Holy Spirit."
She will give birth to a son. Name him Jesus. For he will save his people from their sins.
All this was to happen as the Lord had said he would. He said through the prophet,
The virgin girl will give birth to a son. She will bring forth a male child. And he will be called Emmanuel," (Isaiah 7:14). The name Emmanuel means "God with us."
Joseph awoke. He did what the angel of the Lord commanded him. He took Mary into his house as his wife.
But he did not have marital relations with her until she gave birth to a son. And Joseph called the name of the son Jesus.
The Visit of the Wise Men to Jesus
Jesus was born in Bethlehem of Judea. This took place while Herod was king of Judea. After Jesus was born, wise men from the east came to Jerusalem.
They asked, "Where is the child who was born to be king of the Jews? For we saw his star when we were in the east, and we have come to worship him."
And when Herod heard that, his face was changed and he was disturbed by that, and all Jerusalem was waiting in fear and trembling.
Herod called together all the chief priests and the teachers of the law. He asked them where the Messiah would be born.
"In Bethlehem of Judea," they replied. "For this is what the prophet has written: 'The Lord was pleased to come from his dwelling place in heaven to live on earth. He chose a town in Judea, the small and insignificant town of Bethlehem. From this town he chose to come, the one who is to be our ruler, the one foretold by the prophets of old.'"
"And you, Bethlehem Ephrathah, least of the clans of Judah, from you shall come forth for me one who will be ruler over Israel, whose origin is from of old, from ancient times." (Micah 5:2)
Then Herod secretly called the wise men. He learned from them the time when the star had appeared.
Send them to Bethlehem. And he said, "Go! Search carefully for the child. And when you have found him, bring me word. Then I can go and worship him too."
After the sage had listened to the king, they set out on their way. Ahead of them went the star which they had seen when they were in the East. Finally it stopped over the place where the child was.
And when they saw the throne advancing with them, and it had become illuminated for them from behind them a way.
The wise men came to the house. There they saw the child with his mother Mary. They bowed down and worshipped him. Then they opened their treasures. They gave him gold, frankincense, and myrrh.
But God warned them in a dream not to return to Herod. So they returned to their country by another route. Jesus' family flees to Egypt
When the wise man left, Joseph had a dream. In the dream, an angel of the Lord appeared to him. "Get up!" the angel said. "Take the child and his mother and flee to Egypt. Stay there until I tell you to return. Herod is going to look for the child. He wants to kill him."
Joseph awoke. During the night, he left for Egypt with the child and his mother Mary.
They remained there until King Herod died. Then the word of the Lord spoken through the prophet came true. He had said, "I have decided to bring my son out of Egypt." (Hos 11:1)
Herod realized that the wise men had deceived him. He became furiously angry. He issued orders concerning Bethlehem and the surrounding area. All young boys who were under the age of two were to be killed. This corresponded to the time when the wise men had seen the star.
In this way, the words of the prophet Jeremiah were fulfilled. He had said,
A voice is heard in Ramah. It is the voice of weeping and great sorrow. Rachel weeps for her children. She refuses to be comforted, because they are gone." (Jeremiah 31:15) The Return of Jesus' Family to Nazareth
After Herod's death, Joseph saw a dream while still in Egypt. And in the dream, an angel of the Lord appeared to him.
The angel said, "Arise, take the newborn and his mother, and go with them into the land of Israel. And whoever attempts to kill the newborn, that one has died."
Then Joseph arose, and took the Child and His mother Mary, and returned with them to the land of Egypt.
But then he heard that Archelaus was king of Judea. Archelaus was ruling in place of his father Herod. This made Joseph afraid to go there. After being warned in a dream, Joseph returned to the land of Galilee instead.
There he lived in a town called Nazareth. So what the prophets had said about Jesus was true. They had said, "He will be called a Nazarene."
John the Baptist paves the way.
In those days John the Baptist came and preached in the wilderness of Judea.
He said: "Repent to God, for the kingdom belongs to God, near to those who turn to Him."
John is the one about whom the prophet Isaiah spoke. He said, "A voice of one calling in the wilderness, 'Prepare the way for the Lord; make straight paths for him.'" (Isaiah 40:3)
John's clothes were made of camel hair. He had a leather belt around his waist. His food was locusts and wild honey.
The people went out to him from Jerusalem and all Judah, and also from all the region around the Jordan River.
When they confessed their sins, John baptized them in the River Jordan.
John the Baptist, the son of Zechariah and Elizabeth, his birth a miracle foreshadowing the Messiah, lived in the wilderness, a voice crying out, preparing the way, his mission to point to Jesus, the Lamb of God, his baptism a sign, his testimony powerful, fearless in truth, until his calling complete.
Produce a fruit indicating that you have left your sins.
Do not suppose that you can say, 'Abraham is our father.' I say to you, God is able from these stones to raise up children to Abraham.
The sword is already laid at the roots of the trees. All the trees that do not bear good fruit will be cut down. They will be thrown into the fire.
I will wash you with water to cut you off from your sins and I will call you to repentance. But after me, one will come who is stronger than me, and I am not worthy to carry his sandals. He will anoint you with the Holy Spirit and with fire.
His rod is in his hand to clean the straw from his ground. He will gather his grain into the granary. But he will burn the straw with the unquenchable fire. "Baptism of Jesus"
Jesus came from Galilee to the Jordan River. He wanted to be baptized by John.
But John tried to stop him. He told Jesus, "I need you to baptize me. So why are you coming to me?"
Jesus answered: "Leave her alone like that. It is right for us to do it this way. She is fulfilling the holy plan of God." Then John agreed.
As soon as Jesus was baptized, he went up from the water. At that moment, the heavens were opened. Jesus saw the Spirit of God descending upon him like a dove.
A voice from heaven said, "This is my son, whom I love; I am well pleased with him."
Jesus is tempted.
The Spirit of God led Jesus into the wilderness. There the devil tried to tempt him.
After forty days and forty nights of fasting, Jesus became hungry.
The wicked one came to him. He said, "If you are the Son of God, command this stone to become bread."
Jesus answered, "It is written: 'Man shall not live by bread alone, but by every word that proceeds from the mouth of God.'" (Deuteronomy 8:3)
Then Satan took Jesus to the holy city. He set him on the highest pinnacle.
"If you are the Son of God," he said, "throw yourself down, for it is written: 'He will command his angels concerning you, and they will lift you up in their hands, so that you will not strike your foot against a stone.' (From Psalm 91:11-12)
Jesus answered, saying, "It is written, 'You shall not test the Lord your God'" (Deuteronomy 6:16).
Finally, the devil took Jesus to a very high mountain. And he showed him all the kingdoms of the world and their glory.
If you prostrate yourself and obey me, he said, I will give you all this.
Jesus said to him, "Get behind me, Satan! For it is written: 'You shall worship the Lord your God, and Him only you shall serve.'" (Deuteronomy 6:13)
Then the devil came out of Jesus. Angels came forward, taking care of him. Jesus begins to be in greatness.
John was put in prison; and when Jesus heard of it, he withdrew again to Galilee.
Jesus left Nazareth and went to live in the town of Capernaum, which was by the lake in the region of Zebulun and Naphtali.
And in this way, I have made real what the prophet Isaiah said. He said,
Land of Zebulun! Land of Naphtali! Galilee, where non-Jews live! Land along the Mediterranean Sea! Territory east of the Jordan River!
Those who are now living in darkness will see a great light. They are now living in a very dark land. But a light will shine on them. (Isaiah 9:1,2)
From that time, Jesus began to preach. He said, "Repent of your sins! For the Kingdom of Heaven is near." Jesus chooses the first disciples.
Jesus was walking one day on the shores of the Sea of Galilee. There he saw two brothers. They were Simon Peter and his brother Andrew. They were casting their net into the lake. They were fishermen.
"Come, follow me," Jesus said. "I will make you fishers of men."
So they left their nets and followed him immediately.
And from there, he saw two other brothers. They were James the son of Zebedee and his brother John. They were in a boat with their father Zebedee. And while they were preparing their nets, Jesus called them.
They then bade farewell to the sea, their father, and followed Jesus. Jesus heals sick people.
Jesus went throughout all of Galilee. There he taught in the synagogues. He spread the good news of the Kingdom of God. He healed all diseases, pains, and weaknesses that people suffered from.
News about him spread all over Syria. People brought him everyone who was sick with all kinds of diseases. Some were suffering from severe pain. Others were possessed by demons. Some were shaking violently. Others couldn't move at all. And Jesus healed all of them.
Large crowds followed him. Some people came from Galilee, from the region known as the Decapolis, from Jerusalem, from Judea, and from the region beyond the Jordan River.
Jesus gives blessings.
Jesus saw the crowd. He went up on a mountain and sat down. His disciples came to him.
Then he began to teach them. He said:
Blessed are the people of need who turn to God. Whether the King of the heavens owns them is the same.
Blessed are those who are watchful in prayer. They will be given a reward.
Blessed are the meek. They shall inherit the earth.
Congratulations to the people of hunger and thirst for what is good; so make them more of it from it.
Blessed is the most merciful of the merciful. Those who showed mercy will be shown mercy.
Blessed are the lovers of God, who He has rescued from the darkness. They will see God.
Blessed are the people of peace. For they are the children of God.
Blessed are those who suffer in the cause of justice. For theirs is the kingdom of heaven.
Blessed are you when people mock you and harm you for my sake. And blessed are you when they bully you and tell you all kinds of lies for my sake.
Rejoice and be glad. Your reward in heaven is great. Likewise, people hurt prophets who lived long ago. Salt and light.
You are the salt of the earth. But if the salt loses its saltiness, what good is it? It is no longer good for anything, except to be thrown out and trampled underfoot.
You are the light of the world. A city on a hill cannot be hidden.
Furthermore, people don't light a lamp and put it under a bowl. Instead, they put it on its stand. Then it illuminates everyone in the house.
Similarly, let your light shine before others, that they may see your good deeds and glorify your Father in heaven. Jesus gives a complete meaning to the law.
Do not suppose that I have come to abolish the Law or the Prophets; I have not come to abolish them, but to fulfill them.
What I am about to tell you is true. Heaven and earth will pass away, but not the smallest letter or stroke of the pen will disappear from the law, until everything is accomplished.
Do not break even one of the least important commandments. And do not teach others to break them. If you do that, you will be called the least important people in the Kingdom of Heaven. Instead, practice and teach these commandments. Then you will be called important in the Kingdom of Heaven.
Behold, I say to you, it is necessary that you be more righteous than the Pharisees and the teachers of the law. For if you are not, you will certainly not enter the kingdom of heaven. You shall not murder.
I heard what was said to the people who lived a long time ago. It was said to them: "You shall not murder (Exodus 20:13). Whoever murders will be judged for it."
But here is what I tell you. Do not be angry with your brother. Everyone who is angry with his brother will be judged. Again, everyone who says to his brother, "You fool!" must stand in the Sanhedrin court. But whoever says, "You fool!" will be in danger of the fire of hell.
Imagine that you are offering your gift at the altar. And you remember that your brother has something against you.
Leave your gift before the altar. First, go and be reconciled to your brother; then come and offer your gift.
Imagine someone has a claim against you, and they take you to court. Settle the matter quickly. Do it while you are still with him on your way. If you do not do it, he may hand you over to the judge. The judge may hand you over to the officer. And you may be thrown into prison.
What I'm going to tell you is true. You're not leaving until you pay the last penny! Adultery.
You have heard that it was said, "You shall not commit adultery." (Exodus 20:14)
But here is the advice I give you. Do not look at a woman, even from a distance. Whoever looks at her in a wrong way, has already committed adultery with her in his heart.
If your right eye causes you to sin, tear it out and throw it away. For your eye has within it flesh and blood; and God, if He wills, will forgive you. God desires to lighten your burden; God does not desire to bring any hardship to you.
If your right hand causes you to sin, cut it off and throw it away. For it is better for you that one of your members should perish than that your whole body should go into hell. Divorce.
They said, 'O Moses, indeed some of our people take to excess in the matter of the cow, and you bring them to us.'
But that's what I'm saying. Anyone who divorces his wife allows her to commit adultery. And anyone who marries the divorced woman commits adultery. A man may only divorce his wife if she has been faithful to him. Oath.
And again, you have heard what was said to your people long ago. They were told: "Do not break the covenant you have made with the Lord your God. You must keep the terms of the covenant you entered into with him."
But that's what I'm telling you. Don't make promises like that at all. Don't make them in heaven's name. That's God's throne.
Do not make it in the name of the earth. That is the footstool of God. Do not make it in the name of Jerusalem. That is the city of the great King.
And do not swear by your heads. You cannot even make one white or black hair.
Let "yes" mean "yes." Let "no" mean "no." Anything more than this comes from the devil. Be kind to others.
You have heard that it was said, "An eye for an eye and a tooth for a tooth" (Exodus 21:24; Leviticus 24:20; Deuteronomy 19:21)
But here's what I tell you. Don't fight back against someone evil. "Imagine someone is hitting you on your right cheek. Offer him your left cheek as well.
If someone takes you to court for your shirt, give him your coat as well.
Imagine someone forces you to walk one mile. Go with him two miles.
Give to those who ask of you, and do not keep ignoring those who want to take something from you. Love your enemies.
You have heard that it was said, "Love your neighbor. (Deuteronomy 19:18) Hate your enemies."
But here's what I tell you. Love your enemies. Pray for those who hurt you.
Then you are the children of the patriarch who is in heaven. "He sends his sun upon the evil and the envious, and sends the rain upon whom he wills of his servants, and withholds it upon whom he wills."
If you love those who love you, what reward will you get from your Lord? For the believers, God considers those who strive and those who are diligent to be equal. God does not like those who are lazy.
If you only greet people of your own nation, what more are you doing than others? Even people who don't believe do that.
Be perfect, just as your heavenly Father is perfect.
Donating to the poor.
Beware of doing righteous deeds before people. Do not do them so that people may see you. Otherwise, your Father who is in heaven will reveal to you how often you have spoken falsely.
If you spend, do not tell what you have spent to those who are near them, from the blind and the lame and the sick. Do not be like those who have made much of it from lies. They speak to the tribes and make much of spending. They want praise from the people. And I am not over you a watcher. They have been given words that are not clear-sighted.
When you give to the poor, do not let your left hand know what your right hand is doing.
Then indeed your charity will be kept secret. Your father rewards you. He sees what you do secretly. Prayer.

If you have prayed, then enter the mosques of God. Indeed, God loves those who fear Him. When you have prayed, wash your faces and your hands to the elbows and wipe over your heads and wash your feet to the ankles. And if you are ill or on a journey or one of you comes from the place of relieving himself, or you have contacted women and do not find water, then seek clean earth and wipe over your faces and hands from it. Indeed, God is ever Pardoning and Forgiving.
If you pray, do not race to your standing as the donkeys race, and do not befriend the evildoers. Indeed, the believers are brothers, so make reconciliation between your two brothers, and fear Allah that you may succeed.
Don't be like them. Your father knows what you need even before you ask him.
Thus you should pray: 'Our Father who art in heaven, Hallowed be thy name.
Let your kingdom come. Let your will be done on earth as it is in heaven.
Give us this day our daily bread.
Forgive us our trespasses, as we forgive those who trespass against us.
Deliver us from the nearfall into transgression when we are tempted. And remove us from the devil.
He is Forgiving towards people for their sins, even if they repeatedly commit them. And indeed, you are of a great moral character. Indeed, Allah does not forgive association, but He forgives what is less than that for whom He wills. And if you die in a state of having associated with Allah, you will have no one with Allah to act as an intercessor. Those who ascribe a son to Me - I will indeed forgive them their sin; and I will indeed admit them to gardens beneath which rivers flow; wherein they will be adorned with bracelets of gold and will be dressed in green garments of silk and brocade; they will recline therein upon couches. And how beautiful will be the spouses! This is the Paradise which the righteous have as their heritage. And this is the truth, firm and free from doubt. And they said, "The Most Merciful has taken a son." Exalted is He; He is the King, the Holy, the Source of Peace, the Guardian of Faith, the Exalted in Might, the Possessor of Glory. Exalted is He; He is the Lord of the Great Throne. And they have taken, other than Him, gods whom they do not worship except out of reliance on fate. And they have taken, other than Him, gods in order, perhaps, to be guided. And they have taken, other than Him, gods to whom they do not render worship except out of reliance on fate. And when Our verses are recited to them, they say, "We have certainly heard. If we wished, we could have recited it like it. This is only the myths of the former peoples." And when Our verses are recited to them, they say, "We have certainly heard. If we wished, we could have recited it like it. This is only the myths of the former peoples." And when Our verses are recited to them, they say, "We have certainly heard. If we wished, we could have recited it like it. This is only the myths of the former peoples." And when Our verses are recited to them, they say, "We have certainly heard. If we wished, we could have recited it like it. This is only the myths of the former peoples." And when Our verses are recited to them, they say, "We have certainly heard. If we wished, we could have recited it like it. This is
But if you do not forgive men their trespasses, neither will your Father forgive your trespasses. Fasting.
Indeed, during your fasting, if you take a bath, that does not nullify your fast. This is because the principle of fasting is to abstain from food and drink, and from marital relations. Taking a bath during the day does not fall under any of these prohibited categories. Therefore, it is permissible for a fasting person to take a bath during the day, and this action does not break their fast.
But if you are going to fast, anoint your head with olive oil; and wash your face.
Then no one knows that you are fasting except your father, who is in the heavens. Indeed, your father, for whom is the watching station, is surely aware. So whoever wishes to do you good, he surely knows what you conceal and what you reveal. But whoever wishes to do you harm, he surely knows that you are fasting. And Allah is Knowing of the believers. And He knows what you eat and what you store in your homes. No one knows them except you. And no one has a god with a right to intercession except one for whom the Most Merciful has given permission. And warn your tribe, the near ones.
Do not make the treasures of the earth your own. Then the spiders, the deaf, and the thieves would come and take them.
But lay up for yourselves treasures in heaven, where neither moth nor rust spoils, and where thieves do not break in or steal.
Your heart will be where your treasure is.
The eye is like a lamp for the body. Imagine that your eyes are good. Then your whole body will be filled with light.
But if your eyes are weak, your whole body will be dark. And if the light within you is darkness, then it is pitch black!
No one can serve two masters at the same time. Either he will hate one and love the other, or he will be devoted to one and hate the other. You cannot serve both God and money. So, don't be worried.
I tell you, don't worry. Don't worry about your life, what you will eat or drink. And don't worry about your body, what you will wear. Isn't there more to life than eating? Are not the things that are more important for the body than clothes?
Look at the birds in the sky; they do not sow or reap, they do not gather into barns, yet your Father in heaven feeds them. Are you not much more valuable than they?
Can you add one hour to your life by worrying?
And why do you worry about clothing? Look at the wildflowers growing. They do not spin or weave.
But that's what I say. Even Solomon in all his glory was not arrayed like these lilies.
And if Allah were to embellish the grass, thus, would He not embellish you, you and Him, He being the best of creators? For indeed, this grass will not remain tomorrow, it will be burned tomorrow. O you disbelievers! Your faith is very weak.
Therefore do not be anxious. And do not say, 'What will we eat?' or 'What will we drink?' or 'What will we wear?'
People who don't believe are chasing all those things. Your heavenly father knows you need them.
But seek first the kingdom of God. Do whatever he tells you to do. Then all these things will be given to you as well.
Therefore, do not worry about tomorrow. Tomorrow will take care of itself. Each day has its own troubles.
Be fair when you judge others.
Do not judge people, and you will not be judged.
You will be held accountable in the same way that you hold others accountable. You will be measured in the same way that you measure others.
You see the log in your friend's eye, but you don't see the log in your own eye.
How do you say to your friend: "Let me take a piece of wood out of your eye"? How do you say this while there is a piece of wood in your eye?
Hypocrite! First, take the plank out of your own eye; then you will see clearly to remove the splinter from your friend's eye.
Do not give what is holy to dogs, and do not throw your pearls before swine, lest they trample them under their feet, and then turn and tear you to pieces. Ask, seek, knock.
Ask and you shall receive, search and you shall find, demand and the doors shall be opened for you.
Everyone who asks receives. Whoever seeks finds. The door will be opened for whoever knocks.
Imagine that your son asked for bread. Which one of you would give him a stone?
Or if one of them asks you about someone, you give him a live one. Do you approach them when someone comes to you seeking forgiveness and plunder, and they follow the footsteps of the Prophet? Whoever follows him, and whoever moves away from him, and whoever moves away from him, and whoever moves away from him, and whoever moves away from him, and whoever moves away from him, and whoever moves away from him, and whoever moves away from him, and whoever moves away from him, and whoever moves away from him, and whoever moves away from him, and whoever moves away from him, and whoever moves away from him, and whoever moves away from him, and whoever moves away from him, and whoever moves away from him, and whoever moves away from him, and whoever moves away from him, and whoever moves away from him, and whoever moves away from him, and whoever moves away from him, and whoever moves away from him, and whoever moves away from him, and whoever moves away from him, and whoever moves away from him, and whoever moves away from him, and whoever moves away from him, and whoever moves away from him, and whoever moves away from him, and whoever moves away from him, and whoever moves away from him, and whoever moves away from him, and whoever moves away from him, and whoever moves away from him, and whoever moves away from him, and whoever moves away from him, and whoever moves away from him, and whoever moves away from him, and whoever moves away from him, and whoever moves away from him, and whoever moves away from him, and whoever moves away from him, and whoever moves away from him, and whoever moves away from him, and whoever moves away from him, and whoever moves away from him, and whoever moves away from him, and whoever moves away from him, and whoever moves away from him, and whoever moves away from him, and whoever moves away from him, and whoever moves away from him, and whoever moves away from him, and whoever moves away from him, and whoever moves away from him, and 