Every tree that does not bear good fruit is cut down and thrown into the fire.
By its fruit you will recognize it.
Not everyone who says to me, 'Lord, Lord,' will enter the kingdom of heaven, but the one who does the will of my Father in heaven.
Many will say to me on that day: "Lord, Lord, did we not prophesy in your name? Did we not cast out demons in your name? Did we not perform many miracles in your name?"
Then I clearly tell them: "I have never known you. Away from me, you evildoers!" The wise builder and the foolish builder.
Everyone who hears these words of mine and does them will be like a wise man who built his house on the rock.
Rain is falling. The water is rising. The wind is blowing and hitting that house. But it is not falling. It is built on the rock.
But everyone who hears my words and does not apply them is like a foolish man who builds his house on sand.
The sky is raining. The water is rising. The wind is blowing and hitting that house. And it falls with a loud noise.
Jesus finished saying all these things. The crowd was amazed at his teachings.
He taught as one having authority. He did not speak as the teachers of the law.
