Jesus reached out his hand and touched the man, and said, "I want to do this. Be 'clean'!" The man was immediately healed of his skin disease.
Then Jesus said to him, "Do not say this to anyone. Go, show yourself to the priest, and offer the sacrifice that Moses commanded." It will serve as proof for them." The Faith of a Roman Centurion
When Jesus entered Capernaum, a Roman centurion came to him. He asked Jesus for help.
"Lord," he said, "my servant is at home and cannot move. He is suffering greatly."
Jesus said, "I will go and heal him."
The captain answered, "Sir, I am not worthy to have you enter my house. But just say the word, and my servant will be healed.
I myself am a man under authority. And I have soldiers who obey my orders. I say to this one, "Go," and he goes. I say to this one, "Come," and he comes. I say to my servant, "Do this," and he does it.
When Jesus heard this, he was amazed and said to those who were following him, "I assure you, truly, there will not be found in Israel a heart like this one."
I tell you, many will come from the east and the west, and will take their places at the feast in the kingdom of heaven. For I tell you that many prophets and righteous men longed to see what you see, and did not see it.
But those who think they belong to the kingdom will be thrown outside, into the darkness. And there they will weep and be sad.
Then Jesus said to the Roman soldiers: "Go! It shall be as you have believed." And his servants were healed at that hour. Jesus heals many people.
And when Jesus entered the house of Simon, he saw the mother of Simon and his wife lying down in the house, and she was afflicted with a fever.
Jesus touched her hand, and the fever left her. She rose and began to serve him.
When evening came, they brought to Jesus many who were possessed by demons. He cast out the spirits with a word. And he healed all who were ill.
He did this to fulfill what the prophet Isaiah had said. He said, "He has borne our illnesses and carried our sorrows" (Isaiah 53:4). Following Jesus is costly.
Jesus saw the crowd that was around him. So he gave his disciples orders to go to the other side of the Sea of Galilee.
Then the teacher of the religious law came to him. And he said: "O teacher, I will follow you wherever you go."
Jesus answered, "The birds have nests, and the foxes have dens, but the Son of Man has nowhere to lay his head."
Another disciple said to him, "Lord, first permit me to go and bury my father."
But Jesus said to him, "Follow Me. Let the dead bury their dead." Jesus Calms the Storm.
Jesus entered a boat. His disciples followed him.
Suddenly, a terrible storm came upon the lake. The waves were breaking over the boat. But Jesus was sleeping.
The disciples got up and woke him. They said, "Lord, save us! We are perishing!"
He answered, "Your faith is weak! Why are you so afraid?" Then Jesus got up and rebuked the winds and the waves, and they became still and there was a great calm.
The students were amazed. They asked, "What kind of man is this? Even the winds and waves obey him!" Jesus heals two men who are controlled by demons.
Jesus arrived at the other side of the lake, in the region of Decapolis. Two men who were possessed by demons met him. They had come from the tombs. The men were so violent that no one could travel on that road.
"Son of God, what do you want with us?" they cried out. "Have you come here to punish us before the time comes for us to be judged?"
It was not far, and there was a large herd of pigs breakfasting.
The demons requested of Jesus: "If you cast us out, send us into the herd of pigs."
Jesus said to them, "Go!" So the unclean spirits came out of the men and entered the pigs. The herd of pigs all rushed down the steep bank into the lake. The pig ran to the muddy bank and fell into the water.
Those who tended the pigs fled. They went to the city and told all this. They told the people what had happened to the men who were possessed by demons.
Then he went out from all the city to meet Jesus. And when they saw him, they besought him that he would depart out of their coasts.
Jesus heals a man who cannot walk.
Jesus entered a boat. He went to the other side of the lake, and came to his own town.
Some men brought to him a man who was paralyzed and could not walk. He was lying on a mat. Jesus saw that they had faith, so he said to the man, "Take heart, son, your sins are forgiven."
Then one of the people of the circle said: "This one says something extremely bad!"
Jesus knew what was in their hearts. And he said, "Why do you think evil in your hearts?
Is it easier to say, "Your sins are forgiven"? or to say, "Rise and walk"?
I want you to know that the Son of Man has authority on earth to forgive sins." Then he spoke to the man who could not walk. "Get up," he said. "Take your mat and go to your house."
The man woke up and went to his house.
When the crowd saw it, they were amazed. And they glorified God, who had given such authority to men. Jesus Chooses Matthew
And from there Jesus stood and looked at a man called Matthew, who was sitting at the tax office. And Jesus said to him, "Follow me." And Matthew rose and followed him.
After that, Jesus had dinner at Matthew's house. Many tax collectors and "sinners" came. They ate with Jesus and his disciples.
The Pharisees witnessed that. So they said to the disciples: "Why does your teacher eat with the sinners and the criminals?"
Jesus heard this. And he said, "Those who are healthy do not need a doctor, but those who are sick do need a doctor."
Go and learn what this means: "I desire mercy, not sacrifice" (Matthew 9:13, quoting Hosea 6:6). "I did not come to gather up those who think they are right with God in order to follow me. I have come to gather up sinners in order to follow me." They ask Jesus about fasting.
