Jesus answered, "How can the guests of the bridegroom mourn while he is with them? The time will come when he will be taken from them; then they will mourn.
There is no one to sew a new patch on an old garment. For the new patch would have no strength to endure on the old garment, and it would make a greater tear.
A dead girl and a suffering woman.
And he was saying this word, "A man, a nobleman, came. And he knelt down before Jesus, and he said, 'For my daughter-in-law, she has just died. But go, and command her to be raised up, and she will live.' "
Jesus woke up and walked with him. His disciples also walked with him.
Suddenly, a woman came from behind Jesus. She had been suffering from a disease that made her bleed. This disease had lasted for 12 years. She touched the edge of his robe.
I thought: "I just need to touch his clothes. Then I will be healed."
Jesus turned and saw the woman. And he said to her, "Woman, do not stop believing. Your faith has made you well." The woman was healed at that very moment.
And when Jesus entered the chief priest's house, he saw there those who were enjoying comfort. And he saw the large crowd.
He said, "Go. The girl is not dead. She is sleeping." But they laughed at him.
After the crowd was sent outside, Jesus entered. He took the girl by her hand, and she arose.
News of what Jesus had done spread everywhere in that region. Jesus heals two blind men.
And Jesus went away from there, and followed him two blind men. And they cried out, saying, "Have mercy on us, O Son of David!"
When Jesus entered, the men who were blind brought him. And Jesus said to them, "Do you believe that I am able to do this?" They said to him, "Yes, Lord."
Then he touched their eyes. And he said, "What you believed in will happen to you."
They now see again. Jesus sternly warned them, "Be sure that no one knows about this."
But they went out and spread the news. They talked about it everywhere in that area.
And while they were going out, another man was brought to Jesus. This man was possessed by a demon that had kept him from speaking.
When the man was about to be stoned, he said to the people, "Why are you about to do this?" The people were amazed and said, "We have never seen anyone like you in Israel."
But the Pharisees said, "He casts out demons by the power of the prince of demons." There are few who are workers
Jesus traveled throughout all the cities and villages. He was teaching in their synagogues, and he was preaching the good news of the kingdom of God. He was healing all kinds of diseases and sicknesses.
When he saw the crowds, a deep sorrow came upon him because of them. They were like oppressed, powerless sheep without a shepherd.
Then Jesus said to his disciples: "The harvest is plentiful, but the laborers are few."
Ask the Lord of the harvest to send out workers into his harvest."
Jesus sends out the twelve disciples.
Jesus called his twelve disciples to come to him. And he gave them authority to cast out demons and to heal every disease.
Here are the names of the twelve disciples. First is Simon Peter, and his brother Andrew. Then comes James, son of Zebedee, and his brother John.
Then Philip and Bartholomew, and John the Baptist, and Thomas, and Matthew the apostles. Then James the son of Alphaeus, and Judas the Zealot.
Others are Simon the Zealot and Judas Iscariot. Judas is the one who will later betray Jesus to his enemies.
Jesus sent out these twelve and gave them orders: "Do not go to Gentiles," he said. "Do not enter any Samaritan town."
Go rather to the people of Israel. They are like sheep that have gone astray.
And when death approaches one of you, let him bequeath to those who are his heirs the Imamate of your community. And speak to one another words of appropriate kindness.
Healed the sick. Raised the dead to life. Make those with skin diseases "clean" again. Expelled demons. You received freely, so give freely.
Do not carry gold or silver or bronze in wallets
Do not take a bag for the trip. Do not take extra clothes, sandals, or walking sticks. The worker should be given what he needs.
When you enter a town or village, look for someone willing to receive you. Stay at that person's home until you leave.
When you enter the house, greet the people who live there.
If that house welcomes you, then bless it with peace. Otherwise, do not bless it.
Some people may not welcome you or listen to what you say. If they do not, shake the dust from your feet as you leave that house or city.
What I am about to tell you is true. On the day of reckoning, it will be easier for Sodom and Gomorrah than for that city.
I am sending you out as sheep among wolves. Therefore be wise as serpents and harmless as doves.
Beware! The men will bring you to the local courts. They will flog you in their churches.
They will be presented to you, protecting and ruling because of me. You will witness against them and against those who are not Jewish.
But when they arrest you, don't worry about what you will say or how you will say it. At that time, the right words will be given to you to say.
It will not be you who speaks, but the spirit of your father speaking through you.
Brothers will deliver brothers to be killed. Fathers will deliver their sons. Sons will revolt against their fathers and kill them.
Tomorrow, all the people will hate you for my sake. But whoever stands firm in their right to the very end will be saved.
When people attack you in one place, flee to another. What I tell you now is true. You will not finish going through the towns of Israel before the Son of Man comes.
A student is not better than a teacher. An employee is not better than his boss.
It suffices for the student to be like his teacher. And it suffices for the slave to be like his master. If the head of the household has been named Belial, then what can the others who live there expect?
Do not fear your enemies. Every secret will be revealed. Every hidden thing will be shown.
What you whispered to me in the darkness, say it in the light. What is deemed unsuitable for the ear, proclaim it from the rooftops.
Fear not those who kill the body and cannot kill the soul; rather, fear the One who is able to destroy both soul and body in hell.
Aren't two sparrows sold for a penny? Yet not one of them falls to the ground outside your father's knowledge.
He even counts every single hair on your head!
Do not be afraid. You are worth more than many pigeons.
And what about the person who says in front of others that they know me? I will also say in front of my father in heaven that I know him.
But what about someone who says in front of others that they don't know me? I will say in front of my Father who is in heaven that I don't know him.
I never thought of coming to reconcile people. I did not come to reconcile. I came ready with the sword.
I have come to reverse " 'children against their parents. Daughters will refuse to obey their mothers. Mothers-in-law will be against their daughters-in-law.
'The enemies of a man are the members of his own household.' (Micah 7:6)
Not worthy of me is he who loves his father or mother more than me. Not worthy of me is he who loves his son or daughter more than me.
And whoever does not take up his cross and follow me is not worthy of me.
If anyone finds his life, he will lose it. And if he loses it because of me, he will find it.
Whoever has received you has received me, and whoever has received me has received the One who sent me.
If the believers do good to a prophet, then for him is the reward of the prophet; and if the believers do good to a pious person, then for him is the reward of the pious.
If someone even gives a cup of cold water to a little child who is following me, what I am going to tell you is true. This person will definitely be rewarded.
Jesus and John the Baptist
Jesus finished teaching his twelve disciples. Then he began to teach and preach in the villages of Galilee.
John was in prison. When he heard what Christ was doing, he sent his disciples to him.
They asked Jesus, "Are you the one who was to come, or shall we look for another?"
Jesus answered, "Go and tell John what you hear and what you see.
The blind see. The disabled walk. Those with skin diseases are healed. The deaf hear. The dead are raised. And the good news is spread among the poor.
Blessed are those who are not deterred by what God has revealed but rather seek from God His bounty through it.
When he had dismissed the disciples, Jesus began to speak to the crowds about John: "What did you go out into the wilderness to see? A reed shaken by the wind? What did you go out to see? A prophet? Yes, I tell you, and more than a prophet. This is the one about whom it is written: 'Behold, I send my messenger before your face, who will prepare your way before you.' I tell you, among those born of women, there is no one greater than John the Baptist. Yet the one who is least in the kingdom of heaven is greater than he." When Jesus finished these words, the crowds were amazed at his teaching.
Except, didn't you go out to see? A man dressed in fine clothes? No. The people who wear fine clothes are in the palaces of kings.
So what have you come out to see? A prophet? Yes, I tell you, and more than a prophet.
He is the one about whom it was written in the book. It says: " 'I will send my messenger to prepare the way before me.' (Malachi 3:1)
What I am about to tell you is true. No one who has ever lived is more important than John the Baptist. But the least important person in the Kingdom of Heaven is more important than he is.
From the days of John the Baptist until now, the kingdom of heaven has been forcefully advancing, and men of force seize it.
All the prophets and the law prophesied until John came.
If you are willing to accept it, John is Elijah who was supposed to come.
Let those who have ears hear.
What can I say about people today? They are like children sitting in the markets and calling out to people. They say,
"We played the flute for you. But you did not dance. We sang for you at a funeral. But you did not grieve."
When he came, he started eating and drinking just as you eat and drink. The people said, "He is lame."
But when the Son of Man came, he ate and drank as you do. And people said, 'This man is a glutton; he is a friend of tax collectors and "sinners." ' But wisdom is proved right by her actions.' Towns that do not move away from sin...
Jesus began to speak against the cities where He had done most of His miracles. The people there had not turned from their sins. So He said,
How dreadful that would be for you, Chorazin! How dreadful that would be for you, Bethsaida! Imagine if the miracles that were performed in you were performed in Tyre and Sidon. They would have repented of their sins long ago. They would have put on black clothing. They would have sat in ashes.
But I tell you this. On the day of reckoning it will be easier for a bird to fly than for you to be saved.
"And you, O Qayfar, will you be raised up to the heavens? No! But you will descend to Hell. And if the wonders that were wrought in you had been ordained in Sodom, they would still be here with us today."
But I tell you this. On the day of reckoning, it will be easier for Sodom than for you. Comfort for every weary one.
At that hour, Jesus said, "I testify to you, Father, that you have revealed to me these realities. You are the God of the heavens and the earth. You have hidden these things from the wise and the learned, and you have revealed them to the little children."
Yes, Aba. That's what I wanted.
