So here is what I say. All sin and every evil word spoken against God will be forgiven. But speaking evil things against the Holy Spirit will not be forgiven.
Whoever speaks a word against the Son of Man, it will be forgiven him. But whoever speaks against the Holy Spirit, it will not be forgiven him, either in this age or in the age to come.
If you make the tree good, its fruit will be good. And if you make the tree bad, its fruit will be bad. You know the tree by its fruit.
O assembly of poisonous serpents! How can it be that you, who are the worst of people, can utter anything good? Your mouths speak out all that is in your hearts.
The righteous man speaks righteous words, and these words are from the righteousness that is in his heart. And the wicked man speaks wicked words, and these words are from the wickedness that is in his heart.
But here's what I tell you. On the day of reckoning, people will be held accountable for every irresponsible word they spoke.
"By your words, you will be condemned or acquitted." The miraculous sign, Yunus.
Some Pharisees and teachers of the law came to Jesus. They said, "Teacher, we want to see a sign from you in heaven."
He replied: "Indeed, the deniers and those who break their oaths hasten for a sign from Him. And no sign will come to them except the sign of Jonah."
Jonah was in the belly of a huge fish three days and three nights. Something like this will happen to the Son of Man. He will spend three days and three nights in the tomb.
The men of Nineveh will stand on the day of judgment with the people who are now living. And the Ninevites will prove that these people are guilty. The men of Nineveh turned away from their sins when Jonah preached to them. And now there is someone here who is more important than Jonah.
The Queen of the South will rise up on the day of judgment against the people who are living now. And she will condemn them. She came from a very long way to hear the wisdom of Solomon. And now there is someone here who is more important than Solomon.
What happens if an evil spirit leaves a man? It wanders in dry areas, looking for a place to rest. But it does not find it.
Then he says, "I will return to the house I left." And when he gets there, he finds the house empty. The house has been cleaned and tidied.
Then the evil man goes away, and takes with him seven spirits worse than himself. They enter and dwell in him. And that man is now in a worse state than before. And thus is the case of the evil people today. The mother of Jesus and his two brothers.
And Jesus was still speaking to the crowds, when his mother and his brothers stood outside. And they wanted to speak to Jesus.
Someone told him: "Your mother and brothers are standing outside. They want to talk to you."
Jesus answered and said, "Who is My mother and who are My brothers?"
Jesus pointed to his disciples. And he said, "Behold my mother! Behold my brethren!"
Anyone who does what my Father in heaven wants is my brother or sister or mother.
The Farmer's Story
On that same day, Jesus left the house and sat by the Sea of Galilee.
Large crowds gathered around him. So he boarded a boat. And he sat in it. And everyone stood on the shore.
Then he told them many things using stories. He said, "A farmer went out to sow his seeds.
Scattering the seeds on the ground. Some of them fell on a path. Birds came and ate them.
Some seeds fell in rocky places, where there wasn't much soil. The plant grew quickly, because the soil wasn't deep.
When the sun came out, it burned the plants. So they dispersed because they had no roots.
Other seeds fell among the thorns; and the thorns grew and choked the plants.
Other seed fell on good soil. It produced crops 100, 60, or 30 times more than what was sown.
He who has an ear, let him hear.
The students came to him. They asked, "Why do you use stories when you talk to people?"
He answered, "You have been given a chance to understand the secrets of the Kingdom of Heaven. This chance has not been given to outsiders."
Everyone who possessed this kind of knowledge was given more than him, rather a lot was given from it, and whoever did not possess this kind of knowledge had taken from him what little he had of it.
This is why I use parables when I speak to people. I say, "They look, but they do not really see. They listen, but they do not really hear or understand."
In it the words of the prophet Isaiah are fulfilled. He said: "'You will hear and not understand, and you will see and not perceive.'"
The hearts of these people have become callous. They barely hear with their ears, and they have closed their eyes. Otherwise, they might see with their eyes, hear with their ears, understand with their hearts, and turn to the Lord, who would heal them. (Isaiah 6:9,10)
But God bless your eyes because they see. And God bless your ears because they hear.
What I am going to tell you is true. Many prophets and righteous people wanted to see what you see. But they did not see it. They wanted to hear what you hear. But they did not hear it.
