They met together in Galilee. Then Jesus said to them: "The Son of Man will be delivered into the hands of men."
They will kill him. And on the third day, he will rise from the dead." So the disciples were filled with great sorrow. Jesus repays the debt of the temple
Jesus and his disciples arrived in Capernaum. There, tax collectors came to Peter. They asked him, "Does not your teacher pay the temple tax?"
"Yes, he does that," he answered. And when Peter entered the house, Jesus spoke first. "What do you think, Simon?" he asked. "From whom do the kings of the earth collect taxes and fees? From their children or from others?"
"From others," Peter answered. "So the children do not pay," Jesus told him.
But we do not want to anger them. Go to the lake and cast your fishing hook. Take the very first fish you catch. Open its mouth. You will find exactly the coin you need. Take it and give it to them as a tribute for me and your brothers.
